# Implementation Plan — Phase 2: Spotify Historical Corpus, Dev Set & Evaluation Pool

Prepare the historical knowledge corpus (target 3,000 conversation groups), development inputs (50 customer messages), and held-out evaluation pool (up to 1,000 conversation groups) for SpotifyCares, adhering to strict partition isolation, language validation, duplicate/leakage prevention, and provenance tracking.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Evaluation Pool Review Group Exclusion**: All 61 conversation groups ever inspected in past review manifests (`original_sampling_manifest.json`, `sampling_manifest_v1.json`, `sampling_manifest.json`, `review_scores.csv`) will be strictly excluded from the evaluation pool to avoid review contamination.
> - **Model Input Isolation**: In `dev_inputs.jsonl` and `eval_pool_inputs.jsonl`, only the target customer turn and its chronological ancestor path are included. The selected brand reply is strictly excluded from input payloads to prevent leakage during inference.
> - **Language Determination**: Determined strictly from the target customer message and its required ancestor context (not the brand reply). Method uses script validation, English stopword ratio, and Latin/Spanish/Portuguese marker discrimination. Uncertain cases will be flagged and documented in `results/phase2/exclusion_summary.json`.
> - **Duplicate Handling**: Normalized exact duplicate customer inquiries across distinct conversation groups are detected before splitting. Groups with exact duplicates are either kept in the same partition or deduplicated to eliminate cross-partition inquiry leakage.

